      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-308151",
      ":question/problem": "A produce distributor has $12,000$ apples from multiple orchards. To estimate the percentage that are certified organic, a random sample was taken. The percentage of organic apples was estimated to be $38%$, with a margin of error of $3%$.\n\nIf $r$ is the actual number of certified organic apples in the shipment, which of the following is most plausible?"
