      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-308165",
      ":question/problem": "A national park survey recorded $24,000$ trees in a management zone. To estimate the percentage that are pine, a random sample was taken. The percentage of pine trees was estimated to be $47%$, with a margin of error of $5%$.\n\nIf $r$ is the actual number of pine trees in the zone, which of the following is most plausible?"
